  <XDFTABLE uniqueid="0x491A" flags="0x0">
    <title>DFCO Full Restore RPM Threshold</title>
    <description>Exact 1ME3B. Address 0x14008; 1 rows x 16 columns; uint8; map confidence candidate. Coolant-indexed lower/full-restore RPM threshold in FUN 00050018. At speed count below 4 it is the lower boundary for class 3. At speed count 4 or above every branch reachable under the stock compile-time flags returns class 3 at or below the effective lower threshold and class 0 only strictly above it. The adjusted result is stored in ffff16aa after coolant floors, runtime offsets, and a conditional minimum of 48 counts or 1200 RPM. Exact stock moving branches ignore upper/intermediate table 0001298c. The target-vehicle capture selected only moving samples, retained stock 000126e4/00012718, changed both restore tables, and eliminated the full 0x3f inhibit mask below 5000 RPM. Because 0001298c is not compared on that branch, this hardware result isolates 00012818 as the operational moving veto. Equality remains class 3, so a raw value of 200 vetoes through exactly 5000 RPM in the quantized coordinate and class 0 begins only above it. Result disposition: inline_comparison. Definition address projected from JK08A 00012818 through JK08A-1ME3B.definition-addresses.csv: the target restore coordinator 0007c1b0 of 564 bytes reproduces the instruction structure of 1ND0A 00077888 and reads the lower table first through 0002aa48; the calibration differs only in the four trailing cells. Static diagnostic context: Engine Coolant Temperature [code, homologous_community, via map evidence: indexed_by].</description>
